# Kebu Builder — next-generation law

Full text: `docs/product/KEBU-BUILDER-NEXT-GEN.md` · References: `docs/reference/README.md`.

## Framing for Cursor (never violate)

**Do not** instruct: “build a Shopify clone.” That produces **Shopify with different colors**.

**Do** instruct:

> Build a **new-generation African commerce + website creation operating system** that **exceeds** Shopify, Wix, Squarespace, and current AI builders **in the areas that matter to Kebu users** — while remaining globally usable.

Shopify, Wix, Squarespace, Canva, Spotify, and Figma = **maturity references** when screenshots/docs are in `docs/reference/` — **not** assumed knowledge from the product name. **Product thinking:** `docs/product/KEBU-BUILDER-PRODUCT-THINKING.md` · **Paste:** `docs/product/CURSOR-BUILDER-INSTRUCTION.md`.

**Goal:** Reproduce **level of product sophistication** — not visual clone. Mature product **feel** = density, hierarchy, states, completeness.

**Reality check:** Those platforms already combine AI site generation, visual editing, ecommerce, marketing, analytics, inventory, SEO, and multichannel selling. Kebu must go **beyond** bolting the same feature set together. Differentiate on: **AI as business agent** (not one-shot generator) · **action-oriented intelligence** (WHAT → WHY → ACT) · **Africa-native commerce adapters** · **Opportunity OS connection** · **design worlds** · **Kebu Business workspaces** · **honest end-to-end engineering**.

**Merchant UX:** Different **pages and workspaces**. The merchant must feel they are **running a business**, not only **editing a webpage**. Kebu Business IA: `lib/navigation/kebu-business-nav.ts` · home `/my-sites/[id]`.

Objective: *Describe the business → beautiful functioning business online → keep building with AI.*

## AI pipeline (not prompt → JSX)

AI must output **structured Kebu schema + design system tokens + IA + pages** — never arbitrary production HTML. Flow: understand business → goals → IA → design world → components → content → commerce hooks → render → critique → persist → hybrid edit.

## Design worlds (not Modern Store 1/2/3)

Templates = **design worlds** (Editorial Atelier, Modern Heritage, Culture Magazine, Gallery, …) where layout and business logic match. Flagship portfolios (May Lecor, K-Direction, DkLNS, Ndaoan) are reference worlds — not generic hero/features/contact stacks.

## Editor target (creative studio)

Center = live site (full bleed on flagships). Left rail = pages + section tree. Canvas click = contextual controls. **Bottom command bar = Ask your site** (agent, not buried in sidebar). Hybrid **AI ↔ manual** always. Not “generic left + canvas + right” as the whole product.

## Five creation modes

AI · Template · Blank (live). Import · Code (**NOT IMPLEMENTED**). Same stack for beginners and developers.

